{"audio": "2peter-01.opus", "voice": "Davis", "duration_ms": 160933, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 2400, "text": "2 Peter, Chapter One."}, {"start_ms": 2400, "end_ms": 17467, "text": "Simon Peter, a servant and an apostle of Jesus Christ, to them that have obtained like precious faith with us through the righteousness of God and our Saviour Jesus Christ: Grace and peace be multiplied unto you through the knowledge of God, and of Jesus our Lord,"}, {"start_ms": 17467, "end_ms": 34667, "text": "According as his divine power hath given unto us all things that pertain unto life and godliness, through the knowledge of him that hath called us to glory and virtue: Whereby are given unto us exceeding great and precious promises: that by these ye might be partakers of the divine nature,"}, {"start_ms": 34667, "end_ms": 38800, "text": "having escaped the corruption that is in the world through lust."}, {"start_ms": 38800, "end_ms": 54400, "text": "And beside this, giving all diligence, add to your faith virtue; and to virtue knowledge; And to knowledge temperance; and to temperance patience; and to patience godliness; And to godliness brotherly kindness; and to brotherly kindness charity."}, {"start_ms": 54400, "end_ms": 61867, "text": "For if these things be in you, and abound, they make you that ye shall neither be barren nor unfruitful in the knowledge of our Lord Jesus Christ."}, {"start_ms": 61867, "end_ms": 69600, "text": "But he that lacketh these things is blind, and cannot see afar off, and hath forgotten that he was purged from his old sins."}, {"start_ms": 69600, "end_ms": 85467, "text": "Wherefore the rather, brethren, give diligence to make your calling and election sure: for if ye do these things, ye shall never fall: For so an entrance shall be ministered unto you abundantly into the everlasting kingdom of our Lord and Saviour Jesus Christ."}, {"start_ms": 85467, "end_ms": 93200, "text": "Wherefore I will not be negligent to put you always in remembrance of these things, though ye know them, and be established in the present truth."}, {"start_ms": 93200, "end_ms": 106267, "text": "Yea, I think it meet, as long as I am in this tabernacle, to stir you up by putting you in remembrance; Knowing that shortly I must put off this my tabernacle, even as our Lord Jesus Christ hath shewed me."}, {"start_ms": 106267, "end_ms": 112133, "text": "Moreover I will endeavour that ye may be able after my decease to have these things always in remembrance."}, {"start_ms": 112133, "end_ms": 121733, "text": "For we have not followed cunningly devised fables, when we made known unto you the power and coming of our Lord Jesus Christ, but were eyewitnesses of his majesty."}, {"start_ms": 121733, "end_ms": 132000, "text": "For he received from God the Father honour and glory, when there came such a voice to him from the excellent glory, This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased."}, {"start_ms": 132000, "end_ms": 136400, "text": "And this voice which came from heaven we heard, when we were with him in the holy mount."}, {"start_ms": 136400, "end_ms": 153467, "text": "We have also a more sure word of prophecy; whereunto ye do well that ye take heed, as unto a light that shineth in a dark place, until the day dawn, and the day star arise in your hearts: Knowing this first, that no prophecy of the scripture is of any private interpretation."}, {"start_ms": 153467, "end_ms": 160933, "text": "For the prophecy came not in old time by the will of man: but holy men of God spake as they were moved by the Holy Ghost."}], "words": [{"t": "2", "s": 0, "e": 1109, "si": 0}, {"t": "Peter,", "s": 1109, "e": 1392, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 1613, "e": 1956, "si": 0}, {"t": "One.", "s": 2138, "e": 2319, "si": 0}, {"t": "Simon", "s": 2640, "e": 2960, "si": 1}, {"t": "Peter,", "s": 3020, "e": 3360, "si": 1}, {"t": "a", "s": 3581, "e": 3601, "si": 1}, {"t": "servant", "s": 3701, "e": 4101, "si": 1}, {"t": "and", "s": 4181, "e": 4281, "si": 1}, {